From 52aff310ff02793b16e2c1e0e07a9d8fa7c16c79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 00:16:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: mt8173: add the frequency hopping
 controller

MT8173 has an FHCTL block at 0x10209e00 and both the binding
(mediatek,mt8173-fhctl, already listed in
Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/mediatek,mt8186-fhctl.yaml) and the
driver support for it already exist -- clk-mt8173-apmixedsys.c has carried
a pllfhs[] table naming every hoppable PLL, including FH(CLK_APMIXED_MMPLL,
FH_MMPLL, 0x9c), since it was written. Only the DT node was missing, so
fhctl_parse_dt() never found anything, every PLL registered with plain
mtk_pll_ops, and the hopping path was dead code.

That is not merely a missing feature: on this SoC it makes clk_set_rate()
on MMPLL silently do nothing. mtk_pll_set_rate() writes a freshly computed
pcw into MMPLL CON1, but the hardware only accepts a CON1 pcw that the
frequency hopping engine has actually ramped the PLL to. Verified on an
MT8173 board (Amazon Fire HD 10 2017): a direct write of an arbitrary pcw
to CON1 is silently dropped, both from the kernel and from /dev/mem, while
a write of the value that FHCTL's MON register currently holds is accepted.
So clk_set_rate() returns 0, mtk_pll_recalc_rate() reads back the old
value, and the caller is told nothing went wrong -- the GPU clock, whose
only consumer is mfg_sel, was pinned at its bootloader rate of 455 MHz with
no way to change it.

With this node, MMPLL registers with mtk_pllfh_ops instead, and
hopping_hw_flow() does what the vendor's mt_gpufreq/mt_freqhopping does:
sync CON1 into the FHCTL DDS, take the PLL under hopping control, request
the new DDS, poll MON, write the achieved value back into CON1 and release
control. Measured on that board via the same register sequence: the GPU
clock moves and the change persists after control returns to CON1 (glmark2
build 68 fps at 253 MHz, 87 at 455, 91 at 598).

Only MMPLL is listed. The other hoppable PLLs are left alone because
nothing in mainline asks to retune them and MMPLL is the one that is
actually broken; SSC is left off (hopping-ssc-percent 0) to keep this a
pure fix.

Signed-off-by: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8173.dtsi | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8173.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8173.dtsi
index 169ba4fd1..9faeb01a2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8173.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8173.dtsi
@@ -618,6 +618,13 @@ apmixedsys: clock-controller@10209000 {
 			#clock-cells = <1>;
 		};
 
+		fhctl: clock-controller@10209e00 {
+			compatible = "mediatek,mt8173-fhctl";
+			reg = <0 0x10209e00 0 0x200>;
+			clocks = <&apmixedsys CLK_APMIXED_MMPLL>;
+			mediatek,hopping-ssc-percent = <0>;
+		};
+
 		hdmi_phy: hdmi-phy@10209100 {
 			compatible = "mediatek,mt8173-hdmi-phy";
 			reg = <0 0x10209100 0 0x24>;
